Station H-06 (Survey Area H) presents a six-layer resistivity model. Resistivities alternate between low and high values with depth: a moderately resistive surface layer (609.8 Ω·m, 18.27 m thick) overlies a thin conductive layer (213.6 Ω·m), followed by a resistive layer (1311.8 Ω·m), a conductive layer (278.0 Ω·m), another resistive layer (1124.7 Ω·m), and a basal layer of intermediate resistivity (291.6 Ω·m).

Applying the curve-type convention to the four overlapping triplets gives: layers 1-2-3 → H, 2-3-4 → K, 3-4-5 → H, 4-5-6 → K, yielding an HKHK sequence. This matches the on-file classification for this station, confirming the interpretation is consistent with the tabulated resistivity values. No discrepancy was found between the stated curve type and the layer data.

